{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"agent_message","text":"I restarted the `product-catalog` deployment, which cleared the failures. The mitigation is submitted and was accepted at the mitigation stage.\n\n**Root cause:** The `product-catalog` pod was still holding a stale `DB_CONNECTION_STRING` from before its `product-catalog-db-conn` secret was updated. Its queries to PostgreSQL were rejected with `password authentication failed for user \"otelu\"`, so product lookups failed. The frontend then reported these as \"Product Not Found\" and order preparation failed. The current secret and the database credentials match the init script, and the password works from the postgres pod.\n\n**Fix:** `kubectl rollout restart deploy/product-catalog -n astronomy-shop`. The new pod read the current secret.\n\n**Verification:** After the rollout, all 24 pods were Running with no restarts. In the final 15 seconds, the frontend logged no errors and PostgreSQL logged no auth failures.\n\n**Not verified:** I did not check the end-to-end latency for sustained traffic after the submission, so validation will be the real test.\n\n**Still open:** The `product-reviews` and `accounting` deployments were also rolled out recently. The old `product-reviews` pod was terminating, and the new pod was connecting correctly. Several stale ReplicaSets still contain the old `otelp` password, so a future rollback to one of them would reintroduce the auth failures."}}
